# DIS build context exclusions.
#
# docker-compose builds DIS with `context: ./dis_backend`, so the repo-root
# .dockerignore does NOT apply here — a root-level rule protects the CAS images
# and silently misses this one.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KNOWN, UNFIXED: dis_backend/.env IS BAKED INTO THE IMAGE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile copies it into a layer. Verified 2026-08-14
# against the built image: /app/.env was present and readable, carrying
# JWT_SECRET, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN, DIS_SERVICE_TOKEN and DIS_BEDROCK_*. Anyone who can pull or
# `docker save` the image has the credentials, and deleting the file in a later
# layer would not remove it — the layer keeps it. The file is gitignored, so
# nothing leaked into git; this is purely a packaging problem.
#
# An `.env` rule here fixes it, and was deliberately NOT added yet, because it
# cannot be verified from outside prod. DIS reads config from TWO places:
#   1. compose `env_file: ./dis_backend/.env`  -> injected as environment vars
#   2. pydantic `env_file = ".env"` (config/settings.py) -> reads /app/.env
# Injected vars win, so (2) only supplies keys absent from (1). Those should be
# the same file — the deploy builds on the prod host — but docker-compose's
# env-file parser and pydantic-dotenv's do NOT agree on every edge case (quoting,
# multi-line values), so a key could in principle resolve from the baked copy and
# not from the injected set. Excluding it blind would take DIS down.
#
# TO FIX, from a shell on the prod host, BEFORE adding the rule:
#
#   docker exec contentai_dis sh -c '
#   miss=0
#   for k in $(grep -oE "^[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*=" /app/.env 2>/dev/null | tr -d "="); do
#     if ! env | grep -q "^${k}="; then echo "ONLY IN BAKED FILE: $k"; miss=$((miss+1)); fi
#   done
#   [ "$miss" = 0 ] && echo OK-safe-to-exclude || echo STOP'
#
# If it prints OK, add `.env` / `.env.*` below and redeploy. If it names keys,
# add those to dis_backend/.env on the host first. Either way ROTATE the
# credentials: every image built so far already contains them.

# Tests are source (they live in git) but nothing in the image runs them: the
# Dockerfile never invokes pytest and the production stage does not install it.
# ~800KB of dead weight and needless read surface in a running container.
tests/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.db
*.sqlite3
venv/
.venv/
env/
logs/
*.log
data/
uploads/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# WSL/NTFS alternate-data-stream artifacts — 37 of these sit beside real files in
# this tree. Untracked, meaningless to Linux, and pure build-context weight.
*:Zone.Identifier
